4. Tomcat — JVM heap
For Tomcat, windows_exporter cannot give us JVM heap/GC details. We need the Prometheus JMX Exporter Java agent inside Tomcat. Prometheus recommends the Java-agent mode, and it exposes metrics over another HTTP port such as 9404. Prometheus
The flow will become:
Tomcat JVM
   |
   +--> JMX Exporter :9404
              |
              v
       app01-jmx Service
              |
              v
        ServiceMonitor
              |
              v
         Prometheus


============================

Get tomcat to expose jmx values

& "C:\Program Files\Apache Software Foundation\Tomcat 11.0\bin\tomcat11w.exe" //ES//Tomcat11
Go to java
-javaagent:C:\Monitoring\jmx_exporter\jmx_prometheus_javaagent-1.6.0.jar=9404:C:\Monitoring\jmx_exporter\config.yaml
Apply
Ok
Restart-Service Tomcat11
Test-NetConnection localhost -Port 9404
New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "Tomcat JMX Exporter 9404" -Direction Inbound -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 9404 -Action Allow
============================
oc level
virtctl expose vm windows-2022-appserver \
  --name=app01-jmx \
  --port=9404 \
  --target-port=9404 \
  --type=ClusterIP \
  -n vm-lab

oc label svc app01-jmx \
  app=app01-jmx \
  -n vm-lab \
  --overwrite

oc patch svc app01-jmx \
  -n vm-lab \
  --type='json' \
  -p='[
    {
      "op":"replace",
      "path":"/spec/ports/0/name",
      "value":"jmx"
    }
  ]'

oc run curl-jmx \
  -n vm-lab \
  --image=curlimages/curl \
  --restart=Never \
  --rm -it \
  -- curl -s http://app01-jmx:9404/metrics | head

cat > app01-jmx-servicemonitor.yaml <<'EOF'
apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: ServiceMonitor
metadata:
  name: app01-tomcat-jmx
  namespace: vm-lab
spec:
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: app01-jmx
  endpoints:
  - port: jmx
    path: /metrics
    interval: 30s
EOF

oc apply -f app01-jmx-servicemonitor.yaml
oc get svc app01-jmx -n vm-lab
oc get servicemonitor app01-tomcat-jmx -n vm-lab

test

oc exec -n openshift-user-workload-monitoring \
  prometheus-user-workload-0 \
  -c prometheus -- \
  wget -qO- 'http://localhost:9090/api/v1/query?query=up{service="app01-jmx"}'

oc run curl-jmx \
  -n vm-lab \
  --image=curlimages/curl \
  --restart=Never \
  --rm -it \
  -- curl -s http://app01-jmx:9404/metrics \
  | grep -Ei 'heap|memory|garbage|thread|request|tomcat' \
  | head -80

