Tomcat Heap

For Tomcat heap, let's make your JMX exporter produce clean metric names instead of relying on the current generic rules: - pattern: ".*" setup.
On APP01, replace:
C:\Monitoring\jmx_exporter\config.yaml

with:
rules:

  - pattern: 'java.lang<type=Memory><HeapMemoryUsage>used: (.*)'
    name: jvm_heap_memory_used_bytes
    value: '$1'
    type: GAUGE

  - pattern: 'java.lang<type=Memory><HeapMemoryUsage>max: (.*)'
    name: jvm_heap_memory_max_bytes
    value: '$1'
    type: GAUGE

  - pattern: 'java.lang<type=Memory><HeapMemoryUsage>committed: (.*)'
    name: jvm_heap_memory_committed_bytes
    value: '$1'
    type: GAUGE

  - pattern: ".*"

JMX Exporter specifically supports extracting the HeapMemoryUsage composite values this way and giving them explicit Prometheus metric names. Prometheus
Restart Tomcat:
Restart-Service Tomcat11

Then verify:
Invoke-WebRequest http://localhost:9404/metrics -UseBasicParsing |
Select-String "jvm_heap"

You want:
jvm_heap_memory_used_bytes
jvm_heap_memory_max_bytes
jvm_heap_memory_committed_bytes

